Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Representative calculations", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"0485e05c-bf63-4496-9896-d98d8e07e642"],

Cell["Which stage dominates realistic calculations?", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"134f962b-10da-42d7-ad63-172274f65a83"],

Cell["\<\
Workloads include a vertex trace, a partial bubble and an s-channel tree \
amplitude with polarization tensors. Full adds the complete scalar-projected \
bubble. Construction, export, execution, import and complete \
CalcFormCalculate calls are measured separately. No loop integration is \
performed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e66f594-d58d-4afc-a8ef-f5eb0f470435"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"78e29555-f0f1-4000-add8-7ecdab0ef851"],

Cell["\<\
Use a fresh kernel for reproducible measurements. Mathematica, FeynGrav with \
FeynCalc, and FORM/TFORM are sufficient. No Python, shell scripts or external \
fixtures are needed. Opening this notebook does not execute any cells.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cb338ab8-57a2-42ab-b48f-e0e77d0c9c75"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

